\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

Each native cursor carries a group value and exponents satisfying value=g^a h^b.
A Floyd iteration performs one tortoise update and two hare updates. With the
exact base order, a collision gives a linear congruence. The native solver also
accepts an annihilating multiple and then solves a stronger congruence, which
can discard useful collisions. A nontrivial gcd may produce several candidates,
each actually verified. The original base6 modulo104729 has order5512, while the
supplied104728 is an annihilating multiple, so a verified exponent need not
uniquely identify the original secret. The original six-prime first-collision
study now uses the same native update kernel and reports completed iterations
separately from its old zero-based index.

$$ g^a h^b=g^A h^B\quad\Longrightarrow\quad (a-A)\equiv x(B-b)\pmod{\mathrm{ord}(g)}. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pollard_rho_log_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/discrete_log.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto target = dm::algorithms::mod_pow(2, 17, 1019);
    auto t = dm::algorithms::pollard_rho_log_trace(2, target, 1019, 1018);
    std::print("\n| actual Floyd iteration | cursor | branch | value before | a before | b before | value " "after | a after | b after |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < std::min<std::size_t>(6, t.steps.size()); ++i) {
        auto &r = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   r.iteration, r.hare ? "hare" : "tortoise", r.branch,
                   r.before.value, r.before.a, r.before.b, r.after.value,
                   r.after.a, r.after.b);
    }

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual initial cursor value\n{}",
                       t.steps[0].before.value));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual first tortoise update\n{}",
                       t.steps[0].after.value));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual collision-solver outcome\nfound={}, exponent{}",
                       t.run.found, t.run.exponent));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pollard_rho_log_tiny.svg");
}
```
