> API and interpretation

Every block is a complete editable C++ program. Reusable searches, walks,
geometry decisions, fixture histories and algorithm work live in the canonical
library. Captured records own their values and are not reconstructed by a second
algorithm in the report. Explicit policies count the documented selected calls,
records or scalar entries; they are not peak-byte or wall-clock budgets.
Original reference curves are labelled as references, and finite returned
results are not promoted into universal convergence, recovery, scaling or speed
guarantees.

Python exact powers check every captured multiplicative state and branch,
collision residue/gcd decisions and verified returned equations. Frozen
comparisons preserve three hundred ordinary seeded solver results; a verified
exponent does not identify the original secret uniquely. The shared batch
passes83 native regression tests,18 directly instrumented sanitizer tests,84
compiled and executed public examples,391/391 scoped documentation definitions,
standalone and installed header checks, a linked installed consumer and ten
representative symbol hovers. All four complete programs execute and their
computed results and local figures survive HTML and Markdown export. Build
receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-284-293/`.
